WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(instrumental music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.175
- [Narrator] This is Garret.

00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:03.905
A Sandhill crane.

00:00:03.905 --> 00:00:06.595
If it wasn't for the
Maryland Zoo in Baltimore,

00:00:06.595 --> 00:00:09.512
he probably wouldn't be here today.

00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:17.257
Garret was found wandering
around a Home Depot parking lot

00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:20.086
before being rescued by the zoo.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:23.163
Scattered throughout Western
and Central North America,

00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:27.674
it is incredibly rare to see
them as far east as Maryland.

00:00:27.674 --> 00:00:30.043
In the winter, they migrate south,

00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:32.642
all the way down to Northern Mexico.

00:00:32.642 --> 00:00:34.475
Tall, gray, and slender,

00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:38.072
Sandhill cranes have long legs and necks.

00:00:38.072 --> 00:00:40.473
Their large wingspan make
them incredibly skilled

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.640
soaring birds.

00:00:43.122 --> 00:00:46.535
They breed and forage in
open fields and wetlands

00:00:46.535 --> 00:00:49.707
and can often be seen
visiting farmer's fields

00:00:49.707 --> 00:00:52.508
on the hunt for leftover seeds.

00:00:52.508 --> 00:00:54.657
While their population has rebounded

00:00:54.657 --> 00:00:56.221
in the last few decades,

00:00:56.221 --> 00:00:58.574
loss of habitat and climate change

00:00:58.574 --> 00:01:00.741
are still looming threats.

00:01:02.151 --> 00:01:04.401
This is the Sandhill crane.

